message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "El Escudo: anatomía de una búsqueda pre-registrada y auditada adversarialmente de edge retail en cripto (2018-2026) / The anatomy of a pre-registered, adversarially audited retail edge search in crypto"
authors:
  - family-names: "Castellanos Macias"
    given-names: "Ricardo"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21229491
repository-code: "https://github.com/RicardoCastellanosTrader/el-trading-no-existe-evidencia"
version: "1.0.4"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - backtest overfitting
  - retail trading
  - cryptocurrency
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
  - selection transfer
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered, adversarially audited case study (18 experiment families,
  a search space of 20.9 million configurations crossed with each symbol's
  28-32 presets, Binance top-45 - spot 1h candles for the main search and
  11 of the 18 families, USDT-M perpetuals for the other 7, live execution
  on BingX USDT-M perpetuals -, 2018-2026, taker costs): transfer of
  past-performance selection to another data source is approximately nil
  (rho -0.05 on Binance futures candles over the same window vs +0.60
  in-sample; that interval includes both 0 and +0.30: an underpowered test
  that shows neither a collapse nor a transfer), and no genuine signal
  cleared the bar set for it (magnitudes below costs or below the trivial
  benchmark). Open artifacts, regeneration scripts and real-money execution
  logs included.
